# Fresh Start physics firewall

When porting features from the parent Biomechanics Sandbox into Fresh Start:

## Never

- Copy or adapt parent `physics.ts`, `physicsConstants.ts`, `aero.ts`, `hingeStops.ts`, `solidSegments.ts`, or parent physics smoke/calibration artifacts
- Use parent decision logs / flight audits / feel notes to retune Fresh Start constants
- Port parent `neat.ts` — keep Fresh Start MLP + GA
- Step Rapier with variable/render dt; bypass the fixed-dt accumulator
- Scatter new physics magic numbers outside `src/physics/constants.ts`
- Apply muscle/world forces without `resetForces`/`resetTorques` each physics step
- Introduce unseeded `Math.random` on physics or brain evaluation paths
- Change collision groups without deliberately extending the spawn/world scheme

## Always

- Rewrite selected features against Fresh Start modules (`creature/`, `physics/`, `brain/`, `editor/`, `sim/`)
- Gate unfinished ports behind `src/port/featureFlags.ts` (default off)
- For new Rapier capabilities: write an ADR from `docs/CAPABILITY_ADR_TEMPLATE.md` first
- Run `npm run smoke:all` after physics-adjacent changes
- Only implement IDs marked `[x]` in `FEATURE_PORT_CHECKLIST.md`

Selection source of truth: `FEATURE_PORT_CHECKLIST.md`  
Backlog: `FEATURE_PORT_BACKLOG.md`  
Firewall doc: `docs/PHYSICS_FIREWALL.md`
